To get there, players may do any of the following:
* [[Minigame Teleport]] to [[Trouble Brewing]].
*Drink some [[Rum (Trouble Brewing)|rum]] which can be bought from [[Honest Jimmy]] for 20 [[pieces of eight]] or from the [[Grand Exchange]].
*Use the [[ectophial]] to travel to [[Port Phasmatys]] and then talk to [[Bill Teach]] to sail there.
*Use the [[charter ship]] to sail there.
*Teleport there using a [[Mos le'harmless teleport]] scroll, and then walk to the cave.
*[[Harmony Island Teleport]] (requires [[Arceuus spellbook]], completion of [[Great Brain Robbery]]) and talk to [[Brother Tranquility]].

==Strategy==
While cave horrors will always use their special attack when a [[witchwood icon]] is not being worn, wearing one will make them alternate randomly between kicking every 4 ticks, and screaming every 5. When fighting cave horrors, players will need to either use [[Protect from Melee]] to negate all damage, or wear a witchwood icon and [[armour]] that provides high [[Magic]] [[Defence]] bonus (such as [[dragonhide armour]]) against their special and [[Magical melee|magic-based melee]] attacks. Wearing a witchwood icon is necessary if not using Protect from Melee, as otherwise players will take heavy damage from the special attacks over time.
[[File:Cave horror safespot 1.png|alt=Location of one of the safespots in the Mos Le'Harmless cave, near the entrance. Two cave horrors stand on each side, unable to reach the player.|left|thumb|One of the safespots located next to the entrance of [[Mos Le'Harmless Cave|Mos Le'Harmless cave]].]]
Cave horrors have fairly low [[Hitpoints]], and they are relatively spread apart, so it is generally best to use a fast-firing [[Ranged]] weapon like a [[toxic blowpipe]], [[hunters' sunlight crossbow]], [[magic shortbow (i)]], or [[Karil's crossbow]]. If using Melee, it is recommended to use equipment that provides high Prayer bonus (such as [[proselyte armour]]) and always use Protect from Melee so a better amulet can be used. A [[dwarf multicannon]] can also be used to speed up kills. Cave horrors can alternatively be [[safespotted]] by using the mushrooms, stalagmites, and boulders inside the cave, such as the area by the swamp near the cave entrance.

When cannoning, consider using a [[bonecrusher necklace]], which will comfortably maintain Protect from Melee without using any supplies, as the cave horrors drop big bones. 

Consider bringing a [[log basket]] or a [[plank sack]] with [[Plank Make]], to store the unnoted Mahogany logs they frequently drop in a single inventory slot. 

Switching to the [[Arceuus Spellbook]] and bringing runes for casting [[Adept Reanimation]] should also be considered for passive prayer training as [[ensouled horror head]]s are frequently dropped.


'''Note:''''' It is advisable to keep the witchwood icon in case of a close combat encounter if safespotting, or in case you run out of Prayer points.''
